# Line endings are load-bearing in this workspace, so they are pinned rather than
# left to each clone's `core.autocrlf`.
#
# NOTE ON SCOPE: this file governs `cutdown/**` only. The GENERATED mirror it talks
# about lives at `.claude/skills/cutdown-*/SKILL.md`, ABOVE this directory, and is
# covered by the repo-root `.gitattributes` instead — a distinction the first version
# of this header got wrong, claiming protection it did not provide.
#
# `cutdown skills sync` GENERATES `.claude/skills/cutdown-*/SKILL.md` and
# `skills/registry.json`, and it decides two things by comparing text:
#
#   1. ownership — a mirror is safe to prune only if its body starts with the
#      generated banner anchor (`---\nname: `), and
#   2. staleness — `--check` passes only if the file on disk equals what the
#      generator would write.
#
# This repo has `core.autocrlf=true`. Without the rules below, a fresh clone gets
# CRLF in the working tree while the generator emits LF, so EVERY generated mirror
# would be misclassified as hand-written (never pruned, reported as a problem) and
# `skills sync --check` would be permanently stale on a tree nobody had touched.
#
# The comparisons in `skills-sync.ts` are ALSO newline-insensitive — this file plus the
# repo-root one fix the cause for their respective halves, that fixes the symptom, and
# neither alone is enough: an attributes file cannot retroactively fix an existing
# checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Content-addressed and byte-compared: never translated.
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf

# Media fixtures and anything hashed with sha256 must round-trip byte-exactly.
*.mp4   binary
*.mov   binary
*.wav   binary
*.m4a   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
